1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:01:00,320
== Official Website www.kissasia.co  ==

2
00:01:09,190 --> 00:01:14,830
[Connecting to You]

3
00:01:23,680 --> 00:01:24,970
Finally found you.

4
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:29,780
The person whose thread is tied to me.

5
00:01:32,870 --> 00:01:34,130
Don't come any closer,

6
00:01:34,410 --> 00:01:35,800
you pervert.

7
00:01:35,930 --> 00:01:37,150
Listen to me.

8
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:38,680
If you come any closer,

9
00:01:39,970 --> 00:01:41,000
I'll shoot.

10
00:01:44,479 --> 00:01:46,310
Calm down and listen to me.

11
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:16,600
Lin Jiakai, you're here.

12
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:20,720
I just sang all night, and I'm exhausted.
Let's get breakfast later.

13
00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:22,550
Why are you wearing sunglasses?

14
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:25,810
Where did you buy them?
I've never seen you wear them.

15
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:34,370
Nothing.

16
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:37,230
Are you okay, Chaonan?

17
00:02:37,110 --> 00:02:39,940
[The Second Thread]

18
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:39,750
Are you trying to murder me?

19
00:02:39,970 --> 00:02:46,920
[Murphy's Law:
The One I Avoid Keeps Showing Up]

20
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:47,980
Are you crazy?

21
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:52,640
You don't think threads just pop up
from bumping into me, do you?

22
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:54,390
I just wanted to see

23
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:56,890
if a thread would form between us.

24
00:02:58,240 --> 00:02:59,090
You don't think wearing sunglasses

25
00:02:59,090 --> 00:03:01,680
and not seeing the thread
makes everything fine, do you?

26
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:03,540
Didn't you say the thread
wouldn't just disappear?

27
00:03:03,540 --> 00:03:04,500
Keep your voice down.

28
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:07,700
I don't care! I'm going to scold you
for another half hour!

29
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:08,800
Sorry about that.

30
00:03:10,370 --> 00:03:12,110
Don't be so loud.

31
00:03:14,060 --> 00:03:16,060
I just don't get it.

32
00:03:17,590 --> 00:03:20,100
That's why I wanted
to bump your head and try.

33
00:03:20,710 --> 00:03:21,910
Why would a thread be formed

34
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:23,770
between the skeptical cop and me?

35
00:03:24,460 --> 00:03:26,970
And it shows a color
I've never seen before.

36
00:03:27,410 --> 00:03:28,670
What color?

37
00:03:31,540 --> 00:03:32,650
Grey.

38
00:03:32,870 --> 00:03:34,490
But it's a bit bright,

39
00:03:34,890 --> 00:03:36,640
almost silver.

40
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:38,860
And then?

41
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:43,130
After the thread was formed, I...

42
00:03:44,690 --> 00:03:45,720
What are you doing?

43
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:46,930
It really is a thread.

44
00:03:47,020 --> 00:03:48,240
What thread?

45
00:03:49,660 --> 00:03:51,170
My very first thread…

46
00:03:52,090 --> 00:03:53,640
and it's with you?

47
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:54,829
What do you want?

48
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:58,670
I then asked if I could go home with him.

49
00:03:58,970 --> 00:04:00,100
Pervert.

50
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:02,910
I was just too excited at the moment.

51
00:04:03,930 --> 00:04:04,700
And then?

52
00:04:06,340 --> 00:04:10,210
After that, the student
explained to the skeptical cop

53
00:04:10,300 --> 00:04:12,560
that I didn't actually ask him for money.

54
00:04:12,570 --> 00:04:14,450
So he let me go for now.

55
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:15,750
Thank goodness.

56
00:04:16,209 --> 00:04:18,170
But I followed that cop all the way

57
00:04:18,290 --> 00:04:20,550
until he returned to the police station.

58
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:22,100
Oh my god.

59
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:25,210
You're not just
a sunglasses-wearing pervert;

60
00:04:25,210 --> 00:04:26,690
you're a pervert with bangs,

61
00:04:26,690 --> 00:04:28,770
and a stalking pervert.

62
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:33,740
I just wanted to figure out

63
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:36,220
what was going on
with the thread between us.

64
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:37,720
Let me tell you.

65
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:39,659
If you want to be with him so much,

66
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:42,100
go commit a crime, say, rob a bank.

67
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:43,460
After he arrests you
and takes you to the station,

68
00:04:43,460 --> 00:04:45,310
you can be with him happily forever.

69
00:04:45,310 --> 00:04:47,150
Who wants to be with him?

70
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:50,430
Fine, let's stop talking and eat.

71
00:04:51,580 --> 00:04:54,950
The food here is pretty good, right?
Chaonan.

72
00:04:56,430 --> 00:05:05,990
[Qishi Police Station]

73
00:04:58,110 --> 00:04:59,710
What exactly am I doing?

74
00:05:37,670 --> 00:05:38,670
You again.

75
00:05:39,190 --> 00:05:41,010
What are you doing sneaking around?

76
00:05:41,010 --> 00:05:42,150
Nothing.

77
00:05:42,170 --> 00:05:43,140
I just...

78
00:05:43,730 --> 00:05:46,790
This is someone else's e-scooter.
I saw the keys, so...

79
00:05:47,159 --> 00:05:48,810
My phone is ringing.

80
00:05:49,850 --> 00:05:50,790
I'm leaving now.

81
00:05:51,050 --> 00:05:52,380
You dropped something.

82
00:05:52,680 --> 00:05:53,680
Hey!

83
00:05:59,980 --> 00:06:00,750
[Lin Jiakai]

84
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:02,530
It's Jiakai's?

85
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:03,650
Yeah.

86
00:06:03,750 --> 00:06:05,370
Where did you find it?

87
00:06:05,370 --> 00:06:07,540
I found it at the entrance
of my police station.

88
00:06:07,540 --> 00:06:10,010
Okay, I'll let him know
to come pick it up.

89
00:06:10,790 --> 00:06:13,660
I wanted to ask you something.

90
00:06:14,020 --> 00:06:15,540
Did you know that Lin Jiakai

91
00:06:15,540 --> 00:06:19,300
does psychic readings
at a street stall for people?

92
00:06:19,330 --> 00:06:21,290
Yes, the Psychic Club.

93
00:06:23,250 --> 00:06:24,400
So you allow that?

94
00:06:24,420 --> 00:06:26,440
Yes, because it's not just Jiakai
who's doing it.

95
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:29,400
Some other students also read Tarot cards,

96
00:06:29,420 --> 00:06:31,240
do Mayan‑calendar readings,
or give Reiki sessions,

97
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:33,659
and work with Human Design,
Akashic Records, and things like that.

98
00:06:33,659 --> 00:06:35,750
Our department is quite open to students

99
00:06:35,750 --> 00:06:37,550
doing broad‑ranging research.

100
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:42,400
How interesting.

101
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:44,840
I'll leave it to you then.

102
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:45,420
Thank you.

103
00:06:45,420 --> 00:06:46,330
Thanks.

104
00:06:54,870 --> 00:06:55,690
Ms. Peggy.

105
00:06:55,970 --> 00:06:58,530
Jiakai, come here. Put the report down.

106
00:06:58,540 --> 00:07:01,370
[Psychology Department Lab]

107
00:06:58,810 --> 00:06:59,480
Have a seat.

108
00:07:00,150 --> 00:07:02,010
Put your bag down and do me a favor.

109
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:03,230
What favor?

110
00:07:03,820 --> 00:07:05,140
I've been learning to write lyrics lately,

111
00:07:05,140 --> 00:07:06,370
but I'm completely stuck.

112
00:07:06,370 --> 00:07:08,370
Give me some nouns related to love.

113
00:07:08,370 --> 00:07:10,030
I want them to be abstract. Go.

114
00:07:10,870 --> 00:07:13,760
But I don't know much
about love, Ms. Peggy.

115
00:07:13,780 --> 00:07:16,310
Nonsense. Aren't you
the darling of the Psychic Club?

116
00:07:16,310 --> 00:07:19,110
Don't people come to you
asking about love all day?

117
00:07:19,210 --> 00:07:21,550
A lot of people do ask, but...

118
00:07:21,570 --> 00:07:23,320
it also brings a lot of trouble.

119
00:07:24,470 --> 00:07:26,260
Really? How so?

120
00:07:30,870 --> 00:07:32,930
I encountered a troublesome person.

121
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,290
This troublesome person

122
00:07:37,290 --> 00:07:40,890
must make it tough for you,
keeping your heart itching every day.

123
00:07:41,050 --> 00:07:43,510
Why are you suddenly
saying this, Ms. Peggy?

124
00:07:44,620 --> 00:07:45,500
Your eyes

125
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:48,320
keep looking up in the same direction,

126
00:07:48,340 --> 00:07:50,620
which means you're thinking
about the same thing.

127
00:07:50,620 --> 00:07:51,780
Right?

128
00:07:52,550 --> 00:07:54,680
No, no.

129
00:07:54,750 --> 00:07:55,659
-No.
-Right? Who is it? Come on.

130
00:07:55,659 --> 00:07:56,909
Ms. Peggy, it's not like that.

131
00:07:56,909 --> 00:07:58,370
-Flirting?
-No.

132
00:07:58,370 --> 00:07:59,500
It can't be unrequited love, right?

133
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:01,410
It's an annoying person.

134
00:08:01,410 --> 00:08:03,700
And you kind of like them.
You're keeping secrets.

135
00:08:03,700 --> 00:08:06,630
-Not at all. Don't look at me like that.
-Impossible.

136
00:08:07,440 --> 00:08:08,630
Bingo!

137
00:08:09,140 --> 00:08:10,950
Ms. Peggy, I'll come see you tomorrow.

138
00:08:10,950 --> 00:08:12,500
You're really not being a good friend.

139
00:08:12,330 --> 00:08:13,970
[Psychology Department Lab]

140
00:08:12,530 --> 00:08:13,860
I'm going to be late.

141
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:16,170
At least help me think of some lyrics.

142
00:08:53,940 --> 00:08:55,660
Is it far?

143
00:08:55,690 --> 00:08:57,290
I'm not sure.

144
00:08:58,540 --> 00:09:01,280
I'm definitely following
the thread tied to you.

145
00:09:03,630 --> 00:09:05,370
Are we not there yet?

146
00:09:05,390 --> 00:09:07,080
I'm not sure about the distance.

147
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:08,470
I'll definitely help you find him.

148
00:09:08,470 --> 00:09:09,790
Be a little more patient.

149
00:09:09,790 --> 00:09:11,250
Are you sure?

150
00:09:11,270 --> 00:09:13,540
Are we just going in circles?

151
00:09:13,540 --> 00:09:15,370
Can you really see it?

152
00:09:15,370 --> 00:09:17,280
It's probably because the other person
is also moving,

153
00:09:17,280 --> 00:09:19,630
so the direction of the thread
keeps changing.

154
00:09:19,630 --> 00:09:21,210
You'd better be serious.

155
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:22,830
Or you'll prepare
to compensate me 300,000.

156
00:09:22,830 --> 00:09:23,870
You pervert.

157
00:09:23,910 --> 00:09:25,120
You're so fierce.

158
00:09:28,420 --> 00:09:31,770
Ride faster. My grandpa
rides faster than you.

159
00:09:43,950 --> 00:09:45,150
Where are we?

160
00:09:45,170 --> 00:09:46,910
It's so remote.

161
00:09:47,570 --> 00:09:51,030
Shh? Why would Jeff be here?

162
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:54,460
Yujing, it is him.

163
00:09:54,640 --> 00:09:56,500
Your thread is tied to him.

164
00:09:58,070 --> 00:09:59,610
The internet is down.

165
00:09:59,630 --> 00:10:01,230
Mine too.

166
00:10:01,260 --> 00:10:03,470
He's Jeff?

167
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:06,180
He looks nothing like his photo.

168
00:10:07,710 --> 00:10:09,230
He's pretty handsome.

169
00:10:09,620 --> 00:10:11,880
What are you doing? Keep your voice down.

170
00:10:16,900 --> 00:10:17,950
What now?

171
00:10:18,500 --> 00:10:21,950
I have his contact. I'll message him.

172
00:10:23,390 --> 00:10:24,930
Business is here.

173
00:10:25,790 --> 00:10:27,270
He replied.

174
00:10:28,190 --> 00:10:30,170
Wait, let me try calling him.

175
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:36,670
-Hello?
-Baby, are you busy?

176
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:39,360
Oh, a little. I'm about to have a meeting.

177
00:10:39,380 --> 00:10:40,340
What's wrong?

178
00:10:40,660 --> 00:10:44,440
I asked you about the money earlier.
What happened to your grandpa?

179
00:10:45,260 --> 00:10:46,200
My grandpa

180
00:10:46,220 --> 00:10:48,410
was rushed to the ICU
in the middle of the night yesterday.

181
00:10:48,410 --> 00:10:51,260
It's a bit hard to get
the medical fees together right now.

182
00:10:51,260 --> 00:10:52,800
Where are you now?

183
00:10:54,230 --> 00:10:57,560
I'm at a cafe right now. Why? Miss me?

184
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:59,310
Is this the cafe you were talking about?

185
00:10:59,310 --> 00:11:00,560
Idiot. Jerk!

186
00:11:00,590 --> 00:11:01,730
Give me back my 300,000!

187
00:11:01,730 --> 00:11:02,500
Who are you?

188
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:05,330
Your precious baby, Yujing.

189
00:11:18,290 --> 00:11:19,340
My 300,000!

190
00:11:22,090 --> 00:11:23,090
Let go!

191
00:11:28,350 --> 00:11:30,040
You even called the police?

192
00:11:30,700 --> 00:11:31,960
I'm dead. I'm dead.

193
00:11:39,050 --> 00:11:40,160
Why are you here?

194
00:11:40,830 --> 00:11:43,160
To see if you guys were doing
anything bad.

195
00:11:43,900 --> 00:11:46,130
You followed me?

196
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:49,830
You followed me?

197
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:51,480
Don't flatter yourself.

198
00:11:56,710 --> 00:11:57,800
Unbelievable.

199
00:11:59,000 --> 00:11:59,890
Miss,

200
00:12:00,290 --> 00:12:01,620
say it again—

201
00:12:01,640 --> 00:12:03,020
how did you find them?

202
00:12:03,300 --> 00:12:06,260
Jiakai said he could see some threads.

203
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:07,520
-What threads?
-What threads?

204
00:12:07,520 --> 00:12:09,240
Quiet over there.

205
00:12:09,270 --> 00:12:10,610
You explain.

206
00:12:11,660 --> 00:12:12,660
-Me?
-Right.

207
00:12:13,720 --> 00:12:15,490
Okay, the so-called threads

208
00:12:15,530 --> 00:12:18,840
are like the Matchmaker's red threads,
and various relationship‑binding threads.

209
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:21,980
They are bonds between people—threads
for father‑son ties, mother‑child bonds,

210
00:12:21,980 --> 00:12:23,260
and even the umbilical cord
counts as one such thread.

211
00:12:23,260 --> 00:12:24,330
Jiakai has a third eye.

212
00:12:24,330 --> 00:12:27,160
He can see where you scam syndicates live.

213
00:12:27,190 --> 00:12:29,900
So he wanted us to come find you.
Is that right?

214
00:12:29,920 --> 00:12:33,210
-You believe this nonsense?
-We haven't questioned you yet.

215
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:34,580
It's true.

216
00:12:34,990 --> 00:12:36,210
That's not the point.

217
00:12:36,240 --> 00:12:37,820
The point is I want to know

218
00:12:37,850 --> 00:12:39,440
how many people these guys scammed

219
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:41,500
and how long they'll be locked up for.

220
00:12:42,940 --> 00:12:44,480
Sit down. Sit down.

221
00:12:46,850 --> 00:12:48,230
Everyone calm down.

222
00:12:48,340 --> 00:12:49,320
You on the side, sit down too.

223
00:12:49,320 --> 00:12:50,520
You, you speak first.

224
00:12:50,730 --> 00:12:52,660
When we were dating,
he said he was in another city.

225
00:12:52,660 --> 00:12:54,580
But I found him in this city.

226
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:55,240
I took a plane.

227
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:57,110
He even told me he was at a cafe,

228
00:12:57,130 --> 00:12:58,300
but he was sitting in that...

229
00:12:58,300 --> 00:12:59,080
Long-distance relationship.

230
00:12:59,080 --> 00:13:00,860
Then let's check the plane tickets
and train tickets.

231
00:13:00,860 --> 00:13:01,530
Sure, go ahead.

232
00:13:01,530 --> 00:13:02,490
Need help?

233
00:13:04,660 --> 00:13:07,040
No need. It's just a small scratch.

234
00:13:07,040 --> 00:13:09,570
I'll put some medicine
and slap a band‑aid on.

235
00:13:10,870 --> 00:13:13,200
You look like
you got beat up pretty badly.

236
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:15,150
Not that badly.

237
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:17,730
Just got pushed down a couple of times.

238
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:29,760
Did we know each other?

239
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,600
Perverted College Student.

240
00:13:34,790 --> 00:13:36,750
Is this how you hit on people?

241
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,910
I wasn't trying to hit on you.

242
00:13:39,910 --> 00:13:42,170
I've never hit on anyone, okay?

243
00:13:47,010 --> 00:13:48,470
You have a nosebleed.

244
00:13:50,250 --> 00:13:50,910
That's a lot.

245
00:13:50,910 --> 00:13:52,000
Blood?

246
00:13:50,940 --> 00:13:51,830
[Secure Custody Area]

247
00:13:52,230 --> 00:13:54,760
Don't look, Chaonan.
You're afraid of blood.

248
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:55,880
That's a lot.

249
00:13:57,630 --> 00:13:58,930
That's a lot. That's a lot.

250
00:13:58,930 --> 00:14:01,850
[Secure Custody Area]

251
00:14:06,760 --> 00:14:08,500
We thank Lin Jiakai

252
00:14:08,500 --> 00:14:10,990
for helping the police fight crime

253
00:14:11,010 --> 00:14:12,200
and bust the scam ring.

254
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:14,480
On behalf of the Qishi Police Station,

255
00:14:14,580 --> 00:14:17,110
I present
this certificate of appreciation.

256
00:14:20,750 --> 00:14:22,460
Three, two, one.

257
00:14:23,250 --> 00:14:25,770
Okay. The photos are taken. Thank you.

258
00:14:27,620 --> 00:14:29,470
All right, go do your work.

259
00:14:31,790 --> 00:14:35,620
Jiakai, I heard from my colleague
that you were initially

260
00:14:36,290 --> 00:14:39,250
identified by the victim
as an accomplice of the scam ring.

261
00:14:39,250 --> 00:14:40,120
Yeah.

262
00:14:40,120 --> 00:14:43,120
There was a bit of a misunderstanding
at first.

263
00:14:44,250 --> 00:14:47,250
Fortunately, the truth was found out.

264
00:14:48,510 --> 00:14:50,510
It's strange. Why are you so brave?

265
00:14:50,750 --> 00:14:54,540
How were you bold enough to charge
straight into the scam‑ring's hideout?

266
00:14:54,540 --> 00:14:55,500
No.

267
00:14:55,500 --> 00:14:57,370
I was the one who got beaten.

268
00:14:57,370 --> 00:14:59,000
You're very brave.

269
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,370
We need to learn from you in the future.

270
00:15:01,370 --> 00:15:02,270
I admire you so much.

271
00:15:02,270 --> 00:15:07,310
-If we have similar cases in the future—
-Chief, I've got a school class later.

272
00:15:07,340 --> 00:15:08,760
